\begin_layout Section
Comparative statics without differentiating the policy
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Let 
\begin_inset Formula \[
V(\theta)=\max_x f(x;\theta)
\;\text{subject to}\;
s(x;\theta)\ge0,
\; h(x;\theta)=0.
\]
\end_inset

At a regular point where the value function is differentiable, the envelope formula is 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation}
\boxed{
V_{\theta}
=f_{\theta}(x^*;\theta)
+\lambda^{*\top}s_{\theta}(x^*;\theta)
+\nu^{*\top}h_{\theta}(x^*;\theta).}
\label{eq:envelope}
\end{equation}
\end_inset

There is no 
\begin_inset Formula $dx^*/d\theta$
\end_inset

 term. Optimality makes the first-order effect of the induced policy change vanish.
\end_layout

