\begin_layout Section
The water-filling reduction
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
For a separable resource-allocation problem 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\max_{x\ge0}\sum_{i=1}^n u_i(x_i)
\quad\text{subject to}\quad
\sum_{i=1}^n p_ix_i\le m,
\]
\end_inset

fix a tentative shadow price 
\begin_inset Formula $\lambda$
\end_inset

. Each choice can then be solved independently: 
\begin_inset Formula \[
x_i(\lambda)
\in\arg\max_{x_i\ge0}
\{u_i(x_i)-\lambda p_ix_i\}.
\]
\end_inset

For differentiable, strictly concave 
\begin_inset Formula $u_i$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula \[
x_i(\lambda)=
\begin{cases}
0,&u_i'(0+)\le\lambda p_i,\\[2pt]
(u_i')^{-1}(\lambda p_i),&u_i'(0+)>\lambda p_i.
\end{cases}
\]
\end_inset

Now solve only the scalar resource-clearing equation 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\boxed{\sum_i p_ix_i(\lambda)=m.}
\]
\end_inset

The left side is nonincreasing in 
\begin_inset Formula $\lambda$
\end_inset

 and strictly decreasing on the relevant interior segments, so bisection is reliable when a closed form is unavailable. Corners are selected automatically.
\end_layout

