\begin_layout Section
From a heuristic FOC to a corner-safe method
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
A consumer has wealth 
\begin_inset Formula $w=24$
\end_inset

. She invests 
\begin_inset Formula $\alpha\ge0$
\end_inset

 dollars in a risky asset and 
\begin_inset Formula $\beta\ge0$
\end_inset

 dollars in a safe asset: 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\alpha+\beta\le24.
\]
\end_inset

The safe gross return is 
\begin_inset Formula $1$
\end_inset

. The risky gross return is 
\begin_inset Formula $1/2$
\end_inset

 in state 
\begin_inset Formula $L$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $7/4$
\end_inset

 in state 
\begin_inset Formula $H$
\end_inset

, each with probability 
\begin_inset Formula $1/2$
\end_inset

. Bernoulli utility is 
\begin_inset Formula $u(c)=\sqrt c$
\end_inset

. State consumption is 
\begin_inset Formula \[
c_L=\frac{\alpha}{2}+\beta,
\;
c_H=\frac{7\alpha}{4}+\beta,
\]
\end_inset

so expected utility is 
\begin_inset Formula \[
F(\alpha,\beta)
=\frac12\sqrt{c_L}+\frac12\sqrt{c_H}.
\]
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection*
Step 1: write the marginal utilities
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\begin_inset Formula \[
F_{\alpha}
=\frac{1}{8\sqrt{c_L}}+\frac{7}{16\sqrt{c_H}},
\;
F_{\beta}
=\frac{1}{4\sqrt{c_L}}+\frac{1}{4\sqrt{c_H}}.
\]
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection*
Step 2: write compact KKT
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Let 
\begin_inset Formula $\lambda\ge0$
\end_inset

 be the wealth multiplier. Then 
