\begin_layout Subsection*
Step 4: solve only the implied equalities
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Subtract the two asset conditions: 
\begin_inset Formula \[
F_{\alpha}-F_{\beta}
=-\frac{1}{8\sqrt{c_L}}+\frac{3}{16\sqrt{c_H}}=0.
\]
\end_inset

Equivalently, 
\begin_inset Formula \[
3\sqrt{c_L}=2\sqrt{c_H}.
\]
\end_inset

Since the budget binds, 
\begin_inset Formula $\beta=24-\alpha$
\end_inset

 and therefore 
\begin_inset Formula \[
c_L=24-\frac{\alpha}{2},
\;
c_H=24+\frac{3\alpha}{4}.
\]
\end_inset

Both square roots are nonnegative, so squaring is safe: 
\begin_inset Formula \[
9\left(24-\frac{\alpha}{2}\right)
=4\left(24+\frac{3\alpha}{4}\right).
\]
\end_inset

Thus 
\begin_inset Formula $\alpha^*=16$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $\beta^*=8$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

