\begin_layout Standard
Let 
\begin_inset Formula $y$
\end_inset

 be any feasible allocation. For concave differentiable 
\begin_inset Formula $f$
\end_inset

, KKT gives 
\begin_inset Formula $\nabla f(x^*)=A^{\top}\lambda-r$
\end_inset

, with 
\begin_inset Formula $r\ge0$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula $x^*\perp r$
\end_inset

, and 
\begin_inset Formula $\lambda\perp b-Ax^*$
\end_inset

. Therefore 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\begin{aligned}
f(y)-f(x^*)
&\le \nabla f(x^*)^{\top}(y-x^*)\\
&=\lambda^{\top}(Ay-b)-r^{\top}y\le0.
\end{aligned}
\]
\end_inset

This is why the certificate proves global optimality: feasibility makes both remaining terms nonpositive.
\end_layout

